# GitHub engineering

- GitHub is the source of truth. Local folders are temporary clone/runtime only.
- Do not invent a second "main project" outside this repo.
- Work on `feature/*` (or `fix/*`) branches; open PRs. Do not put all work on `main`.
- Use conventional commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, …). No generic messages (`update`, `final`).
- Before coding: read README/ARCHITECTURE, check Issues/branch/pending changes, change only what is needed.
- Never delete or rewrite the whole project to add a feature.
- Never commit secrets or real `.env` values; use `.env.example` and GitHub Secrets.
- Prefer PostgreSQL + versioned migrations; not SQLite as production DB.
- After relevant work: update docs/CHANGELOG when appropriate, push, open PR, wait for CI.
